theory.intro:
A sinusoidal model $y=k\cos(at)+c$ is built from three features of the situation. The **amplitude** $k$ is half the gap between the maximum and the minimum, the **mean position** $c$ sits halfway between them, and $a$ comes from the period.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[-{Stealth}] (-0.3,0) -- (8.4,0) node[right] {$t$};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,0) -- (0,4.8) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[dashed] (0,2.5) -- (8,2.5);
\node[left,font=\small] at (0,2.5) {$c$};
\draw[thick,blue!70!black,domain=0:8,samples=120,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{2.5+1.2*cos(60*\x)});
\draw[<->] (3,2.5) -- (3,3.7) node[midway,right,font=\small] {$k$};
\draw[<->] (0,4.3) -- (6,4.3) node[midway,above,font=\small] {$T$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.question_text:
The graph shows the depth of water at a jetty over $16$ hours, with the mean position drawn as a dashed line.
Find a model $y=k\cos(at)+c$ for the depth $y$ metres, where $t$ is the number of hours after midnight.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[width=10cm,height=6.5cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=-0.6,xmax=17.5,ymin=-0.6,ymax=7.4,xtick={0,2,...,16},ytick={0,1,...,7},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$t$ (hours after midnight)},ylabel={Depth (m)},ylabel near ticks]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,domain=0:16,samples=150] {2*cos(22.5*x)+4};
\addplot[dashed,domain=0:16,samples=2] {4};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A mass hangs from a spring above a bench.
The graph shows its height over $10$ seconds, with the mean position drawn as a dashed line.
Find a model $h=k\sin(at)+c$ for the height $h$ centimetres, where $t$ is the time in seconds.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[width=10cm,height=6.5cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=-0.4,xmax=11,ymin=0,ymax=23,xtick={0,1,...,10},ytick={0,2,...,22},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$t$ (seconds)},ylabel={Height (cm)},ylabel near ticks]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,domain=0:10,samples=150] {6*sin(36*x)+14};
\addplot[dashed,domain=0:10,samples=2] {14};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

mastery.question_text:
The graph shows the volume of air in a person's lungs over $8$ seconds of steady breathing, with the mean position drawn as a dashed line.
Find a model $V=k\cos(at)+c$ for the volume $V$ litres, where $t$ is the time in seconds.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[width=10cm,height=6.5cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=-0.4,xmax=9,ymin=0,ymax=6.6,xtick={0,1,...,8},ytick={0,1,...,6},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$t$ (seconds)},ylabel={Volume (L)},ylabel near ticks]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,domain=0:8,samples=150] {-1.6*cos(45*x)+4};
\addplot[dashed,domain=0:8,samples=2] {4};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
